# 🚀 Enhancing Performance of Phobos in the D Ecosystem

## 📌 About the Project
This project focuses on improving the performance of the Phobos standard library in the D programming language. The goal is to optimize critical components to make them faster, more efficient, and reliable.

## 👤 About Me
I am Cyrus, a student with a Certificate in ICT. I am passionate about programming, problem-solving, and contributing to open-source projects. I am currently applying for Google Summer of Code.

## 🎯 Project Objectives
- Identify performance bottlenecks in Phobos  
- Optimize algorithms and implementations  
- Reduce memory usage  
- Improve execution speed  
- Ensure code maintainability and clarity  

## 🛠️ Technologies Used
- D Programming Language  
- Phobos Standard Library  
- DMD Compiler  
- Dub Package Manager  
- Git & GitHub  

## 📈 Expected Outcomes
- Improved performance of selected Phobos modules  
- Cleaner and more efficient code  
- Better understanding of performance optimization in D  

